  "discussion": "The forecast remains on track for today. A medium period swell out of the north-northwest (325 to 350 degree) will hold through much of the day. This swell will gradually decrease from tonight into Monday before another small to moderate swell fills in Monday night, keeping small to moderate surf in place through Tuesday. A large northwest to north- northwest swell is then forecast to arrive late Wednesday into Thursday and could bring surf near or right at warning levels. A small south-southwest swell will keep surf around the average today before declining Monday through the remainder of the week. Rough surf along east-facing shores will hold at or above seasonal average through this weekend. Surf will decrease slightly by early next week as trades begin to ease before increasing again by Wednesday.",
